;; bin/repr-java attr-check (bin/lib/repr-java/front-check --attr native): by corpus, the forms files that may
;; differ between the conversion of javac's trees and that of the native trees with the native attribution
;; provider ({:CORPUS {:forms #{PATH ...}}}, paths as front-check-known.edn's), and the facts whose native
;; answers may differ from javac on Arbace's ({:CORPUS {:facts {fact count}}}) (doc/classes/JAVA-FRONTEND-SURVEY.md,
;; "As built: JN9a"). None.
;;
;; :bridges (JFS94 (b), "As built: JN9b"): the reads of arbace.repr.java.model that may answer a native object by
;; javac's symbol of the same declaration; a read bridged that is not listed fails the check:
;;   :model/binary-name      a local or anonymous class's binary name: javac numbers them as Attr meets them
;;                           (JFS91 (a): javac's until JN9d)
;;   :model/package-members  the classes of the unit's package as javac's ClassFinder lists them (JFS92 (a))
;;   :model/type             a `var` local's or an implicit lambda parameter's type (inferred, JN9d), a
;;                           multi-catch parameter's (a least upper bound)
;;   :model/const-value      a `var` local's constant (its type inferred)
;;   :model/supertypes       an anonymous class of a diamond (its supertype inferred, JFS76 (a))
{:bridges #{:model/binary-name :model/package-members :model/type :model/const-value :model/supertypes}}
